# 3. Sāmayik — contemporary English↔Sanskrit

**Maheshwari et al.**

arXiv:

`https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.14004`

PDF:

`https://arxiv.org/pdf/2305.14004`

ACL/LREC:

`https://aclanthology.org/2024.lrec-main.1245/`

GitHub:

`https://github.com/ayushbits/saamayik`

Around **53,000 English-Sanskrit sentence pairs**, explicitly intended to represent **contemporary Sanskrit prose** rather than classical verse. Sources include pedagogical materials, tutorials and modern spoken/written material. ([arXiv][3])

They benchmark adaptations of several multilingual pretrained MT models.

Very useful—but it measures almost the opposite distribution from Tantrāloka or the Ṛgveda.

