# 4. Samasāmayik — Hindi↔Sanskrit, 2026

**Karthika et al., 2026**

Paper:

`https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.24307`

HTML:

`https://arxiv.org/html/2603.24307`

PDF:

`https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.24307`

GitHub:

`https://github.com/karthika95/samasaamayik`

**92,196 Hindi-Sanskrit pairs**, including **90,016 training** examples and **1,839 test pairs**. Sources include Spoken Tutorials, Chandamama, Mann Ki Baat and instructional materials. Models benchmarked include ByT5, NLLB and IndicTrans-v2. ([arXiv][4])

