# 7. Chandomitra — semantic fidelity under Sanskrit metrical constraints

Paper:

`https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.00815`

PDF:

`https://arxiv.org/pdf/2506.00815`

ACL 2026:

`https://aclanthology.org/2026.eacl-long.24/`

Chandomitra asks models to produce **structured Sanskrit anuṣṭubh poetry from English**. It therefore separates aspects like syntactic/metre validity from semantic preservation and uses human judgments on roughly a thousand English-Sanskrit pairs to select semantic metrics. ([arXiv][7])

Not a normal Sanskrit→English benchmark, but extremely useful for a **kāvya evaluation layer** because it demonstrates why you need independent dimensions for:

**meaning / grammar / meter / poetic acceptability.**

