# 9. MITRA — Buddhist multilingual evaluation at much larger scale

**Nehrdich & Keutzer, 2026**

Paper:

`https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.06400`

HTML:

`https://arxiv.org/html/2601.06400`

PDF:

`https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.06400`

Repository:

`https://github.com/dharmamitra/mitra-parallel`

Search corpus:

`https://dharmanexus.org`

MITRA has **1,742,786 parallel sentence pairs** involving Sanskrit, Tibetan and Buddhist Chinese, alongside MT and cross-lingual retrieval models. It benchmarks translation from Sanskrit, Pāli, Tibetan and Buddhist Chinese into English. ([arXiv][9])

For Sanskrit evaluation it uses **5,552 Sanskrit-English pairs across several domains**, including Buddhist sūtra material as well as non-Buddhist Vedic/poetic material. Its MT evaluations use GEMBA with an LLM judge. ([arXiv][9])

This and SansTib are the strongest current foundations for a **Buddhist Sanskrit-specific evaluation track**.

