# 11. SAHAAYAK — huge training corpus, weaker as a benchmark

Paper:

`https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.00021`

It contains approximately **1.5 million Sanskrit-Hindi pairs** spanning news, conversation, politics, history, sports and ancient Indian literature. ([arXiv][12])

Excellent for training/data mining.

I would **not** treat “1.5M pairs” as “1.5M benchmark items.” The critical benchmark property is a small, clean, independent and ideally human-verified held-out set.

